schuderfloss@netscape.net (Martin Brodie) wrote in message news:<4bb16963.0208220413.4465ca30@posting.google.com>...
> Came across this situation too. Found no command, but several files
> and settings can be checked for current settings
> 
> 1. /etc/inet.local
>    'man inet.local' for more info
> 2. /etc/rc.config
>    ethernet interface speed may be set in here
> 3. /var/adm/messages
>    may tell you the speed machine negotiated when booted.
> 4. review the settings of ewa0_mode at the chevrons
> 5. good check we use is ftp the latest patch kit (114MB) from another
> server on LAN if it takes approx 10 secs then assume interface =
> 100MBps Full duplex anything else you have problems or are running at
> HALF DUPLEX 10 MBps
> 
> hope this helps
> 
